      en: "The Rössing Uranium Mine, situated in the Namib Desert near Arandis, is one of the oldest and largest open-pit uranium mines in the world. Discovered in 1928, commercial operations began in 1976. The mine is a massive contributor to the Namibian economy, historically accounting for a significant portion of the nation's exports. Due to its immense size, the open pit is visible from space. Over the decades, it has produced hundreds of thousands of tonnes of uranium oxide, cementing Namibia as a leading global supplier of nuclear fuel. Earth Science K6 — uranium extraction.",
